From eb21a7e65259ebe1607d82901dd8f08643b1e7f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Florian Kleber <26285351+kleberbaum@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 08:14:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] feat(plugin): resolve the permissions of the store for
 every plugin

golem run seeds the permissions of the store, but no plugin can ask
whether a sender holds a node, so every plugin would judge a player by
their operator level, and the tools of /golem stay with every operator
of level 2 while the seed grants their nodes golem.* to the group admin
alone.

The runtime now holds a Resolver, the permissions of the store loaded
into golem-permissions, which golem run builds after the seed and which
stops the start when the set of the store does not load. A plugin asks
it through Context::check_permission, which answers whether the sender
holds the node, whether a rule decided and why, and
Context::has_permission, which allocates nothing for a player. The
console holds every node, another source every node from the level 2
and none below it, never one of the player it runs as, and a player
what golem-permissions grants them, whatever their operator level.

A change of the store moves its generation. Resolver::refresh looks at
it under one lock of the store and wakes the thread golem-permissions,
which loads the set and its generation and swaps it in, so a check
never waits for a reload. A set that does not load is logged once and
the checks keep the one they hold.

The tools of operators of /golem take the node golem.<subcommand> that
way, so an operator of the game who is not in the group admin is
refused them, while a command block keeps them.

